Hello,

Further to my previous email
(http://www.spinics.net/lists/linux-sparse/msg03448.html), I have been
working with sparse to print an abstract syntax tree from an OpenCL
kernel code in Json. I made a little program to do this, and it is
something similar to "c2xml.c" or "ast-view.c". Actually, as an OpenCL
kernel is a subset of C, the program seems to work with "traditional"
C code as well. If this patch has any value to sparse (example,
how-to...), you can do what you want with it, and I hope the code
could help someone in the future to understand how sparse is working.
Fabien Cellier (fabien.cellier@gmail.com) and me will maintained the
program.

Regards,
Guillaume Oberl=E9

